A||||8||WisconsinGT||Thoughts from a Fiero owner.||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||09-03-2000||01:14 AM||||Today I went to the local Pontiac dealer. Just to look around at new vehicals. Across the street, is a Toyota dealer. So I go over to look at the new MR2. A salesman approaches and asks if I want to take it for a spin.:-) I agree. WOW! What a great ride. The handling is superior to our Fieros. The downside...the lowend torque is far from perfect. But once you get the RPM's going she really goes. (Typical for Toyotas.) <P>Anyway, this event made me ponder Pontiacs positioning in the sports car arena. The Trans Am to me has a great from end. (Love the Ram Air intakes) But it looks big and bulky. The Sunfire....Well I do not deem it a sports car. The GrandPrix/Am is a family car with some balls. I think the Fiero was the first and last true sports car for Pontiac. I wonder if Pontiacs positioning in the car market changed in 88 and some suit said kill the Fiero.<P>Oh! And let's talk about butt ugly vehicals for a moment. The Aztec has to be close to #1 in that catagory. What in the hell are you thinking Pontiac?<P>Sorry! I had to let off some steam. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||09-03-2000||06:11 AM||||I would have to say that the Aztec ranks right up there with the Pacer in the looks department.Why did that "Truck,Car,MiniVan,SUV" or whatever it is ever make it out of the concept stage?? ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Standard||09-04-2000||05:11 AM||||Pontiac doesn't really <B>have</B> a position in the sports car arena, last I checked.  In fact, I don't think any U.S. auto maker has a position, if you're talking about the 2 seat, affordable, fun to drive kind of sports cars... pretty sad, in my opinion...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||09-05-2000||12:09 AM||||Yep, the Aztec is right up there with the Pacer and Gremlin as far as style goes.  I bet they are trying to keep up with the PT (or potty) Cruiser that I am seeing so much of.  Definitely a retro kind of thing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||09-05-2000||12:52 AM||||I just pulled up beside an Aztec earlier today.  Big, black and white planar slabs. Looked almost homemade. <P>The Sunfire's kind of a cute car, though.  And the PT Cruiser has style - not really <B>my</B> style, but several people I know seem to like it.  It's a vehicle I like to see around, but I don't want one.  Chrysler will probably have a lot of success with it, as long as they keep the quality up.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||09-05-2000||09:36 AM||||"I think the Fiero was the first and last true sports car for Pontiac."<P>Does the GTO count for nothing?!? true, sports car in the late 60's ment something different then what it means today, but the GTO was one of the top dogs back "in the day". other then that, if Pontiac would ever get the Rageous out of concept... it's like a sports car w/ a family hauling pakage. I can't say pontiac makes the best cars, but I like what they produce (with the exception of the Sunbird and 6000) so I'll keep driving them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||09-05-2000||11:06 AM||||I think if the late 90's Sunfires were made just a bit wider (like the concept Sunfire), it would be a decent looking sporty car.  Gosh Pontiac, if you say "Wider is Better" then make'em wider!<P>I don't know who was responsible of the '00 Sunfire refreshen design, but that person killed whatever was left of the car.  The sleek pointed nose replaced with one with puggy squishy cheeks for fog lights at the corners (What is that all about?)<P>For the Aztek, the concept Aztek actually looked pretty cool.  Again, another good concept lost in design.  I'm considered a target buyer for that thing, and I'm not interested in it at all.  I seen early and pre-production models before they were on sale tooling around here spring and all summer and still don't like it.<P>The GTO is definitely a car I'd like to see again, especially bringing back "The Judge"  Jay Bernard's GTO concept was pretty cool.  A few things made the car look dorky, but overall was pretty decent.<P>I still cannot understand why the Aztek got approved before the GTO?  Anyway, my 2 cents.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||09-05-2000||12:47 PM||||I still think the time is right for Pontiac to reintroduce a 2-seat sports car based on existing FWD drivetrains and suspensions.  They couldn't call it "Fiero," of course, but think about how far they've come in terms of reliability and refinement since the X-car.<P>Use a shortened Grand Am platform and plug in the 150-hp 2.4 Twin Cam, the 185-hp 3.4 pushrod V6 and the 215-hp 3.5 "Shortstar" V6.  Doesn't that sound like fun?  The base car would whoop the Miata and MR2; the GT would spank the Honda S2000.  Of course, knowing dumbass GM, you probably wouldn't be able to get the 5-speed with anything other than the 4-banger...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||09-05-2000||01:25 PM||||I saw the Aztek in a magazine, this weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I am <I>not</I> in a hurry to see one in person. It looks like the late 80's Lemans (The Daewoo variety) with a suspension lift.<BR>What in the hell were they thinking?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||13
